  "report_markdown": "DRAFT\n\n**Complaint/History**\n- Diarrhea for the last three days, described as loose and watery stool, occurring 6–7 times per day.\n- Associated lower abdominal pain, localized to the left side, described as cramp-like, coming and going.\n- Initial vomiting at symptom onset, now resolved; vomit was food-colored with no blood.\n- Subjective fever at symptom onset (3–4 days ago), no measured temperature; no current fever.\n- Feels weak and shaky; no night sweats.\n- Loss of appetite; able to tolerate fluids and light foods (soups, smoothies).\n- Symptoms began after eating at a Chinese restaurant four days ago; no other family members with identical symptoms (one child had vomiting only).\n- Symptoms affecting daily life, requiring proximity to toilet; patient has continued going to work (accountant).\n\n**Relevant Background**\n- History of asthma, well-controlled with inhaler.\n- No other known bowel or gastrointestinal conditions.\n- Lives with wife and two children.\n\n**Medications**\n- Inhaler for asthma.\n- No other medications documented.\n\n**Allergies**\n- Not documented.\n\n**Findings**\n- No blood in stool.\n- No blood in vomit.\n- No current vomiting.\n- Pain is localized to left lower abdomen, cramp-like, intermittent, not radiating.\n- No measured fever; patient felt hot at onset.\n- No alcohol use.\n- Non-smoker.\n\n**Clinician's Assessment**\n- Likely gastroenteritis, possibly post-infectious, potentially linked to recent takeaway meal.\n- Viral etiology suspected; bacterial cause not ruled out.\n\n**Plan/Follow-up**\n- Conservative management advised: hydration, use of oral rehydration solutions (e.g., Dioralyte).\n- Paracetamol as needed: up to two tablets four times daily for fever and weakness.\n- Advised to take 2–3 days off work to rest.\n- Review in 3–4 days if symptoms persist; possible stool sample testing if no improvement.\n- No antibiotics prescribed at this time.\n- Patient agrees with plan and has no further questions.",
